Implement Local Play in Alva — Complete Two-Controller Multiplayer System

Objective

Introduce a fully functional Local Play feature to Alva, allowing two people to fight each other on the same device using two separate physical controllers.

This must be a proper extension of Alva’s existing systems, not a separate fighting engine or an imitation of multiplayer.

Local Play must use the same battle mechanics, animations, stages, fighters, physics, scoring, and overall visual identity as the existing game.

The feature must integrate naturally with everything already implemented.

The main requirements are:

1. Introduce a Local play button on the Home Screen, positioned directly beside a half-width Play button.
2. Keep Local play visible at all times, but enable it only when at least two compatible controllers are connected.
3. Give the enabled button the same animated green border glow as the Home Screen’s Download button.
4. Introduce a new Select local mode page, visually identical to the existing Select mode page.
5. Offer only Quick Battle in Local Play for now.
6. Make Local Quick Battle follow this exact sequence:
    * Player 1 fighter selection
    * Player 2 fighter selection
    * Stage selection
7. Create a genuine two-human-player battle, with each player controlling their own fighter independently.
8. Display both fighters’ move HUDs simultaneously, with Player 1 on the bottom-left and Player 2 on the bottom-right.
9. Use prominent, consistent player identification throughout Local Play: Player 1 is RED and Player 2 is BLUE.
10. Preserve all current gameplay features and prevent regressions to Play, Watch Mode, and Practice Ground.

This must be an actual working implementation, including controller handling, navigation, rendering, match lifecycle, edge cases, localization, and tests.

