2. Home Screen — split Play and introduce Local play

Current behavior

The Home Screen has a full-width green Play button, followed by Watch mode, Practice ground, and Discover.

The actions are created inside js/screens/home-screen.js, and their appearance is controlled primarily by css/home.css.

The menu currently uses a grid approximately 320px wide, with consistently sized action buttons.

Required new layout

The first row must contain two buttons displayed horizontally:

┌────────────────────┬────────────────────┐
│ Play               │ Local play         │
└────────────────────┴────────────────────┘
┌─────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ Watch mode                              │
├─────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ Practice ground                         │
├─────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ Discover                                │
└─────────────────────────────────────────┘

The diagram is conceptual; use the game’s existing actual design.

Exact layout rules

* The original Play button should occupy approximately half its previous width.
* The new Local play button must have exactly the same width and height as Play.
* Both buttons together, including their spacing, must occupy exactly the original full-width Play row.
* Both buttons must align perfectly with the left and right edges of the full-width buttons beneath them.
* Use the same vertical height as the current Home Screen action buttons.
* Preserve the existing button border radius, typography, spacing, icons, interaction animations, and focus treatment.
* The existing Play button must remain green.
* Local play must use the same dark/transparent secondary button style as Watch mode, Practice ground, and Discover.
* Local play must not have a green-filled background.
* Keep both buttons readable in English and French.
* Preserve proper sizing on short displays and smaller landscape screens.
* Do not cause the Alva logo or any Home Screen elements to shift off-screen.

Prefer a dedicated two-column row inside .home-actions, using equal-width grid columns, rather than hard-coded button widths.

Update any Home Screen height calculations only if required. The first row must still count as one row, not two.

Controller availability

The Local play button must always exist and remain visible.

However, it must only be actionable when:

* At least two distinct supported controllers are connected.
* At least two of those controllers are active according to Alva’s existing controller limit.
* The browser’s Gamepad API is available and functioning.
* At least one playable fighter is available.

Do not count an unsupported controller as an eligible controller.

Two controllers of the exact same model must count as two separate controllers when they are separate devices.

More than two supported controllers may be connected; Local Play should use two distinct active controllers rather than requiring exactly two total.

Preserve Alva’s existing four-active-controller limit and excessive-controller warnings.

Disabled appearance

When fewer than two eligible controllers are present:

* Show Local play in the correct position.
* Use the existing disabled button appearance.
* Do not show the animated green border.
* Do not allow the button to initiate a Local Play session.
* Keep the label readable.
* Provide a localized explanation such as “Connect two controllers to play locally.”
* Use appropriate accessible descriptions so users understand why the button is unavailable.

The existing Controller Connections dialog should remain accessible and useful for connecting or identifying controllers.

Enabled appearance — green border

This is particularly important.

When two controllers become available, Local play must receive an animated light-green border treatment matching the existing Download button on the Home Screen.

The Download button already implements this in css/home.css, with a pseudo-element, green border, subtle box shadow, and home-download-glow animation.

Reuse those existing design principles and, where possible, existing animation definitions.

The effect should have:

* A green border matching Alva’s established green accent.
* A soft surrounding green glow.
* The same elegant pulse cadence as the Download button.
* No bright green fill.
* No flashing or jarring transitions.
* No layout movement during animation.
* Proper reduced-motion behavior.

Use the Download button’s existing green border and shadow values as the design reference, rather than inventing an unrelated green.

For readability, keep an identifiable green outline in the enabled state even between glow pulses. The animation should enhance the enabled state.

When the second controller disconnects, remove the enabled glow immediately and revert to the disabled appearance.

When it reconnects, automatically update the button again.

Functionality

The existing Play button must continue opening the normal Select mode page.

The Local play button must open the new Select local mode page.

Do not redirect Local play through the existing single-player setup or its Custom Play / Regular Play choice dialog.

