Do not introduce health bars, rounds with separate health pools, or different damage calculations.

Do not change the AI or difficulty systems to support Local Play.

Automatic turn-around

Alva has an existing Automatic turn-around setting that currently applies to the human player.

Both local human fighters should follow the existing setting consistently.

If enabled, both players receive the normal human-player Automatic turn-around behavior.

If disabled, neither receives it.

Do not apply CPU-specific logic to either player.

Combat independence

Make sure every system can correctly identify each fighter’s owner.

This includes:

* Direct melee hits.
* Projectiles.
* Summons.
* Techniques.
* Deflects.
* Shields.
* Status effects.
* Launches.
* Stage hazards.
* Scoring.
* Eliminations.
* Match statistics.

A projectile from Player 2 must belong to Player 2, not Player 1.

An attack landed by Player 1 must be credited to Player 1.

Mirror matches must remain completely independent.

Camera

Continue using Alva’s shared camera.

Both fighters must remain appropriately framed wherever possible.

Do not introduce split-screen gameplay; the two players fight in the same arena and see the same screen.

